  <keyword>nelson.display.DisplayFormatOptions</keyword>
  <short_description>Display format options object.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>fmt = nelson.display.DisplayFormatOptions()</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>fmt = nelson.display.DisplayFormatOptions(Name, Value)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>Name, Value</param_name>
      <param_description>name-value pairs for NumericFormat, LineSpacing, and TruncateMatrices</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>fmt</param_name>
      <param_description>display format options object</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>
      <b>nelson.display.DisplayFormatOptions</b> stores display format options used by <b>format</b>.</p>
    <p>The object has three public properties: <b>NumericFormat</b>, <b>LineSpacing</b>, and <b>TruncateMatrices</b>.</p>
    <p>
      <b>NumericFormat</b> can be <b>short</b>, <b>long</b>, <b>shortE</b>, <b>longE</b>, <b>shortG</b>, <b>longG</b>, <b>shortEng</b>, <b>longEng</b>, <b>+</b>, <b>bank</b>, <b>hex</b>, or <b>rational</b>.</p>
    <p>
      <b>LineSpacing</b> can be <b>compact</b> or <b>loose</b>.</p>
    <p>
      <b>TruncateMatrices</b> can be <b>on</b> or <b>off</b>. In the graphical command window, <b>on</b> truncates large two-dimensional numeric, logical, and sparse matrices when their full display exceeds the visible area.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Save and restore display format.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[oldFormat = format();
fmt = nelson.display.DisplayFormatOptions('NumericFormat', 'longE', 'LineSpacing', 'compact', 'TruncateMatrices', 'on');
format(fmt)
format(oldFormat)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
